WEBVTT

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.160
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:25.380
I heard it
 A voice cursing fate

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:29.550
I found it
 A way to use my power

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.090
What you want are not words,
 are they?

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.760
That love inside
 I want to send it on

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.350
Justice is not on my side

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.350
The only thing absolute for me
 is myself

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.150
Come on Wakers. Ready, go!

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:51.360
Protecting the illusions
 that somebody dreamed of

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:55.700
will liberate the stagnant sky

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:01.540
We hurl our unanswerable cries
 at each other

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:06.370
And they become the reason we live

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:12.050
What can I do in this
 hopeless world we live in?

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.470
Only those that keep searching

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.850
can become the future

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:23.850
Start the revolution!

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:34.690
(They are Always Laughing)

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:41.990
Yes. He looked different,
 but it was Hitoyoshi.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.660
All right. I'll send backup.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.420
No, I can handle it on my own.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:50.170
Please don't tell Miss Kikko.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:54.130
Really?
 But a kid would stand out there.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.170
I'm...

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.680
I got it.
 I know what Hitoyoshi's aim is.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.180
He's a hazard.
 Don't let your guard down.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.640
(Moulin Rouge)

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.730
(Hilarious! The Mountain Horses)

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.440
Hey, wait!

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.740
Stop that Freeze, don't.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.700
Stop it!

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:22.580
Darn it, Freeze!

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.410
What? I'm busy over here.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.420
Hey, stop fooling around.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.010
Excuse me a bit.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.260
Oh gosh.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.430
Cut it out already. Parihi!

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.730
It's the Thunder God.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.690
You idiots!

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.860
So you want to work under us?

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.030
You sure? You'll have to
 carry instruments and stuff.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.620
He won't be able to get beer for us.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.870
So, you like us?

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.130
Yeah. You guys are so funny.
 I love you guys.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.550
We're so happy to have
 so many people here.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.260
We're not here for you.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.470
Get the girls out here.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:25.300
Oh, aren't I good enough?

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:26.310
Sure!

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.270
We, the Mountain Horses,
 have special powers.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.270
Generate electricity.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.810
Move things.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.020
- Liar!
 - You're superhumans?

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:39.320
- We'll call the cops.
 - Oh, a slip of the tongue.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.030
The scary Security Force
 will come for us.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.030
Please keep it a secret.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.540
We, the Mountain Horses,

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.460
gained these special powers
 3 years ago.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.540
That again?

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.380
June 30th of the 41st of Shinka Era.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.340
It was at the Nippon Budokan.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:01.340
The famous Quartet came
 and Japan was in an uproar.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.050
Lots of Japanese singers
 were there to open.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.560
But you must've forgotten.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:17.520
Still the opening act?

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:21.530
They're copying Las Vegas
 with the comedians and stuff.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.860
I went through quite some trouble
 to get these.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.530
Let's enjoy it.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:37.380
Hey, what are you doing?

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.710
He did it.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.050
I didn't do anything.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.510
What the heck?

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.520
We did it.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.270
We played out our skit till the end.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.410
I'm starry.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.450
I mean, I'm sorry.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.090
What's going on?

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.760
They're superhumans.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.680
Those rumors...

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:33.680
They were true.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.270
How do their powers feel like?

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.690
You don't feel anything?

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.610
It's said that their powers
 liberate human souls.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.830
But I'm not human.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.580
I can see it.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.910
The music is a window.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.120
There's a war going on
 somewhere in this world.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.960
I can see into the souls
 of the young soldiers.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.800
I'm not alone.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.590
I'm connected through this universe.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.390
Hey, you're going to
 the Budokan again, right?

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.480
That was just for yesterday.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.440
Oh, then when's your next gig?

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.660
Excuse me a bit.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.290
What the...?

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:35.790
What is this?

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.620
What's going on?

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.920
Honey, what are you doing?

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.170
A nervous breakdown?

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.880
I don't want you disappearing.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.220
Hey, did you talk about it?

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:54.510
You're all still young,
 and can get a new job.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.100
(Sugimoto Productions)

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.560
Um, excuse me a bit.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.150
Good, right there.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.690
A little stronger.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.610
You idiot, that's too strong.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:10.990
Hey, you guys.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.830
Look, Dan.
 Freeze can generate electricity.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.000
- See?
 - And me too.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.160
Parihi.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.670
Watch it, geez.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:31.590
Actually, me too.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.100
This can't be a coincidence.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:44.360
This is the power to liberate the soul
 they talked about?

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.860
Then everyone there would
 have special powers,

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.860
and there'd be chaos.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:51.650
Are you listening, Freeze?

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:53.700
Gosh.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.660
So we're superhumans now.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:00.870
Rainbow Knight and Earth-chan.
 I loved them as a kid.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:03.500
Don't say we've become superhumans.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:05.750
Why not?

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.670
Of course not.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.300
There's the Functional Secrecy Law.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:14.680
The newspaper or radio
 can't report about superhumans.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.510
TV will never call us.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:17.680
You're right.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.310
But now that we're superhumans,

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:24.020
I feel like I can do something
 to bring meaning to my life.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:30.320
Like if there's a bad guy...

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.820
Somebody help! Thieves!

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.070
Hey, Dee!

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.330
Can't be helped.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.830
Wait, you guys.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.120
Stop!

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.720
- Yeah. Dee!
 - Kill them.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.010
What's wrong?

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:00.510
I can't move when I'm like this.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.270
Give him a full round of bullets
 to his guts.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.900
Ouch, it's starting to hurt.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.110
Parihi.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.360
Wait...

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:20.620
He's heavy...

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.450
It's my turn now.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.870
See if you can handle the shock.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.050
My shoulders are light.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.510
My nerve pains are gone.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:36.720
I feel warm all over.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.090
Huh?

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.100
Why'd you heal them, idiot?

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.440
Excuse me a bit!

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:55.360
Gigander Seven!

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:57.610
Secret Detective Team BL!

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.660
Always getting in our way!

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:09.960
I'm sorry.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.880
We couldn't help it.
 Our powers aren't much.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:16.550
Superhumans aren't for us.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.550
We're an embarrassment.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.050
Let's go home.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.520
They can be left alone.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.620
Did you see that?
 This isn't a trick or a manga.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.630
As you know,
 Angel Stars are real superhumans.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.790
And they're girls, dressed like this.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:58.630
Yes, we are
 officially authorized superhumans.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:02.340
I thought superhumans
 fought unnoticed.

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:07.100
I didn't think Teito Publicity
 would promote superhumans.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:10.980
The police and Public Security
 have authorized superhumans.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:15.110
Once the Secrecy Law is amended,
 national projects will be started.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:17.650
The Angel Stars' debut song.

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:21.070
"The Small Glass." Let's hear it!

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.990
(November, the 42nd of Shinka Era
 Sugimoto Productions)

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:29.000
We could've been Japan's first
 superhuman singers.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.330
But we haven't been singing lately.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:35.540
Not just that,
 we're a novelty band now.

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.130
What's wrong with that?

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:40.720
Kids love us.
 We just got a raise, too.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.720
But can we just go on like this?

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:45.050
What do you mean?

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:46.970
Our songs aren't hits.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:51.140
We just joke on stage,
 hit each other, and get laughed at.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:52.810
We're making them laugh.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:55.020
But we're not real comedians.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:56.860
Just second rate.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:59.320
Dee...

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.530
Hey.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:02.820
I brought some coffee.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:04.740
Something wrong?

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.240
Nothing, "Tarofuu."

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:09.740
How's work? It's tough, isn't it?

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:12.500
Not at all.
 It's great being with you guys.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.580
Excuse me, President.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.670
Not here, huh.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.180
Sir, we're thinking about retiring.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:27.510
An advance on our salary?
 6 months worth?

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.810
You're too kind.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.650
Excuse me a bit... Woah!

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:49.370
Ohnaga Confectionery is ready
 to increase production.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:55.830
A drawing for a free
 life-sized poster of the Angel Stars.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.380
This'll be a hit.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.210
The goal is 1 million.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:02.050
But what irony.

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:05.010
Young people who love
 the superhuman Stars

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.340
will lose their superhuman powers.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.010
You mean Neynorine?

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.220
That's it.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:13.140
The Superhuman Factor
 Suppression Drug, huh?

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:16.850
According to Bracks Medicines Co.,
 it's completely harmless.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:19.020
It's safe to put in chocolate.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:21.650
Ever since that concert last year,

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:26.360
more youngsters are playing music and
 saying things like "love and peace."

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.530
And guys growing their hair out.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:32.660
This experiment with Neynorine
 and would-be superhumans...

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.540
The government is curious too.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:39.040
Do you dislike superhumans,
 Ms. Tozaki?

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:40.500
No.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:44.800
I just think they should be managed
 according to the country's needs.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.590
We can't have them multiplying.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:51.680
Mr. Don.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.350
A dog is speaking!

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:55.680
Fuurou...?

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:00.020
Us? Superhumans?

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:02.860
Our job is to protect superhumans.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.860
You don't have to hide it.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.530
You can infiltrate anything, right?

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:10.620
It was great how you went in
 that garbage can.

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:16.000
We heard rumors about Sugimoto
 Productions and sent Fuurouta.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:19.460
Besides being Japan's
 greatest entertainment production,

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:22.130
they use mutants and evil scientists.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:23.840
An evil organization.

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:25.050
That can't be.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.220
We want to know their next step.

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:31.050
Help us as a superhuman.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:35.520
If I did, we'd lose our jobs.

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:38.350
You want to keep playing stupid
 among evil?

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:42.020
Those stupid skits are our job.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.520
Excuse me.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.200
I think we should do it.

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.370
Do what?

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.450
The chocolates at
 Ohnaga Confectionery.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:59.620
We can't let young fans
 eat harmful drugs.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.380
The publicist said it was harmless.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:06.960
We can't let them use innocent people
 as lab rats for some drug.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:09.470
Let alone, preventing superhumans.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.590
Dee.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.800
We can't stay second rate forever.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:15.850
Let's be accepted as superhumans.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:18.430
We could be heroes that
 saved the youngsters.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.690
What's wrong with second rate?
 Is it meaningless?

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:25.020
Is everyone in show-biz first rate?

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:26.570
Are they all superstars?

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:29.240
If not, you can't sing or do comedy?

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:33.280
You're probably too young to remember.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:38.240
Before the war, superhumans were
 always in the papers and magazines.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.790
But that changed with the new law.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.120
Superhumans could be weapons of war.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.290
So they became military secrets.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.000
But that was before.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:50.380
You might be right, but I remember it.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:52.680
So superhumans aren't okay.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.300
It's not funny.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:55.760
What do you mean?

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:58.970
I like it when the audience laughs.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:01.020
Laughter is the key to longevity.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:04.440
We can be second or third rate.
 We can sing or do skits.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.360
That's what I want to do.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:10.360
Even if we became superhumans,
 we'd be second rate superhumans.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.070
Would that be funny?

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:19.490
The Osaka Earth Exposition in 3 years.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:23.160
All the publicity for it will be done
 by Imperial Publicity.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.080
This is the theme song for it.

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.590
You could sell a million,
 no 10 million.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.960
Will you guys sing it?

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:33.720
Incredible.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.340
Why us?

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:36.760
That's because...

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.930
Laughter is universal.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:43.180
I doubt it's a job
 for someone like us.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.060
Isn't it okay if you're satisfied?

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:48.900
You'll be first rate musicians
 without doubt.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:52.740
What was that for, Don?

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:55.400
Why did you send her away?

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:56.910
You're going to decline, aren't you?

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.200
It's not funny.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:01.080
But it's 10 million copies!

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:05.290
She found out about the chocolate
 and came to silence us.

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:08.080
But you don't plan on being
 a superhuman, right?

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:09.590
That's right.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.420
Until now.

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:14.260
But just this once.

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:17.930
If we don't stand up now,
 we'd be lower than third rate!

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:20.720
(Ohnaga Confectionery)

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.560
Excuse me a bit.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:24.730
This feels weird.

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:26.440
Let's go.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:40.910
All right.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:49.580
With all this,
 we won't go hungry for a while.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.920
- Want a bite?
 - Shut up.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:54.630
What is it?

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:57.550
It's moving!

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:00.800
It's getting more like
 an evil organization.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.470
Let's do this, superhumans!

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.730
You distract it. I'll...

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:10.770
No way.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.230
We shouldn't have done this.

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.940
You guys!

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:17.360
Don't hide. Don't push!

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:19.110
- You mean...
 - Like this?

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.070
No!

00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:21.240
Excuse me a bit!

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.700
Great! Now that I'm inside...

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.790
Hal, do your Parihi.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:29.710
Parihi.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.460
Weren't you going to break it?

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.460
I didn't have a chance.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.470
It's getting faster.

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:41.470
What's he doing there?

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:43.100
Pull, Hal!

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.260
All right, got it.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.430
Parihi.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:55.190
Yes! We're like real superhumans.

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:57.190
Oh dear.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:01.280
The novelty band Mountain Horses
 was a facade.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:05.790
But they were actually
 evil destructive superhumans.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.790
We just want you
 and your company to reconsider.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:13.500
One, two, three.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:30.940
Hurry, run.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:32.600
Dee, you too!

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:35.360
Hal, pull me from afar.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.440
Got it.

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:42.700
I'll pull you.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:43.950
Pa...

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.030
...rihi.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.660
If you wouldn't have been so stupid.

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.210
Do it, Freeze!

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:58.590
Really? Okay.

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.170
Shock, shock.

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:11.310
You won't make it in time
 for the drawing now.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:15.310
Shouldn't you hurry on home
 and remake your ads?

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:17.570
Stars!

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:24.570
Superhuman Bureau, Jiro Hitoyoshi.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:26.990
You're from the GaGon case...

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:28.580
We'll take it from here.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.950
It's fine. I'm used to negotiations.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:34.000
Tell the president.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.330
We quit the production today.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:37.420
And?

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:41.460
Promise not to get in our way
 no matter what stage we go on.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:43.760
You're not disbanding?

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:46.970
You can't even get on TV
 without us backing you.

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:48.220
Lose those dreams.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:51.060
It's not like dreaming would kill you.

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:53.850
And quit mixing in weird stuff.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:57.940
Then we won't go show this to anyone.

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:02.030
Thanks.

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:04.360
Hey, where's Dee?

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.620
Oh yeah, our salary advances.

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:11.450
We'll call it even
 as Dee's funeral gift.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:14.580
Mr. Don!

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:17.630
Come with us as a superhuman.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.420
That's not funny.

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:34.890
Looking for a superhuman ally, right?

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:38.350
Yeah, to defeat you guys.

00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:41.650
So, what did Mr. Don and them say?

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:44.860
They're not superhumans
 nor interested in being one.

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:46.320
Stop it!

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:47.740
Geez, Freeze!

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:49.070
A pity.

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:52.950
They could've been great
 superhumans with those powers.

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:56.000
Don't you get it?
 They are superhumans.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:58.750
Look how many are laughing.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:01.170
That's the greatest power of them all.

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:02.750
Fuurouta.

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:05.760
Did you want to be with them instead?

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.760
I'll stay till the end.

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:17.350
I only have one life.

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:18.390
Parihi.

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:20.900
Hey!

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:00.950
This is Human Satellite Earth.

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:03.790
I caught your radio waves
 asking for help.

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:06.630
If you truly desire help, I'll come.

00:24:07.170 --> 00:24:10.380
But, why don't you understand, idiot?!
